==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*8 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn after 73.33 seconds<sup>2,200f</sup>, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Gilgamesh (Enemy)|Gilgamesh]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is pretty easy compared to the one prior. All of the threats spawn on timers, so it can be rushed with fast units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and Money UP combos such as [[Bento Special (Combo)|Bento Special]] and [[Offshore Accounts (Combo)|Offshore Accounts]], which can enter Gilgamesh's blindspot and quickly eliminate him before he or his support could do much.

=== Recommended Units ===

* [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - As mentioned before, Bahamut's extreme speed and raw DPS allows him to easily bypass Gilgamesh's attacks and deal heavy damage from there, especially if Talented with Explosions. Bahamut rushing is still possible on higher difficulties, but something else has to be brought for the Elder Sloth, whose damage (37500/50000 on 2/3-4 Crown) can instantly kill Bahamut and can tank long enough to land at least one attack on him.
* [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]] - An essential unit for 4-Crown, Royal Guard is a surprisingly dangerous melee unit who lands rapid Single Attacks with Massive Damage to Aliens. One can neutralize Mistress Celeboodle on its own, and even a small group will quickly erase Elder Sloth. Speed and Research Combos can be used to great effect on them so enough can sneak past Gilgamesh's fire.

